  "why_it_supersedes": "v1 ran at n_generated=400; the committed kernel froze n=120. v1's all-coupled arm was documented as reproducing the status quo and was never reconciled against it -- at n=400 it reports `both` sd 0.0140 against the grid's own 0.0410. Since the comparison BETWEEN arms was the whole finding, the finding does not survive the geometry correction.",
  "question": "At the committed geometry, which seed roles carry the across-seed spread, does the coupling suppress or inflate it, and is any suppression a statistical relationship or an artifact of three RNGs sharing one integer?",
