  "honest_limits": [
    "Measured on the MARKOV candidate. It bounds the INSTRUMENT's nuisance variance and says nothing directly about the HF generator's own sampling variance. The generator's paired delta IS measurable from the committed grid and is reported in wiki/glm_grid_reconcile_2026-11-21.json instead of being estimated here.",
    "60 replicates per arm. Every arm-to-arm claim is reported as a bootstrap CI on the SD ratio rather than a point value, and a CI containing 1.0 is reported as such.",
    "The anchor is one seed. Arms B, D and E pin the corpus or split at it, so an anchor-specific property would show up as an arm effect; v1 swept the anchor for arm B and found the effect held at 0, 3, 7 and 9, but that sweep was at the wrong geometry and is NOT inherited here.",
    "Arm F changes the fit corpus by a fixed offset, so its fit and eval draws are different but not independent in any stronger sense; it tests whether the matching matters, not how.",
    "The delta experiment uses Markov order 1 as the rival candidate. It establishes what the pairing does to a delta between two CHEAP candidates, which is the instrument question; it is not a statement about a delta between two fine-tuned checkpoints.",
    "One geometry, one organism, one null."
  ],
  "wall_seconds": 578.5
